00:09:46,478 --> 00:09:49,824
And now what is actually spacecraft flight software?

70
00:09:51,982 --> 00:09:54,384
So it's very easy.

71
00:09:54,638 --> 00:09:58,916
Spacecraft flight software is the software which flies on the spacecraft.

72
00:09:59,104 --> 00:10:05,904
So you can imagine that there is some software also on the ground station or let's say on the mission control system.

73
00:10:07,054 --> 00:10:08,704
But that's not the software I'm talking about.

74
00:10:08,784 --> 00:10:17,604
I'm talking about software which is there and communicates via ground antennas with the mission control center.

75
00:10:18,414 --> 00:10:24,772
Just to give very quickly an overview of what that kind of software can do, just that you have some imagination.

76
00:10:25,454 --> 00:10:28,132
So it's in charge of autonomy.

77
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:44,420
So there the most important thing is controlling the attitude and orbit, but also thermal control, managing modes of the spacecraft, like for instance when it's just moving to the target orbit or something like that.

78
00:10:45,664 --> 00:10:56,064
Health monitoring, power generation monitoring and distribution of power, including deployment and rotation of the solar arrays, then communication with ground.

79
00:10:56,144 --> 00:11:08,132
All the telecommands which are sent to the spacecraft are processed by software, and as well, all the messages, what we call telemetry, are sent by software back to ground, so it's a super important feature.

80
00:11:09,230 --> 00:11:10,544
And then mission management.

81
00:11:11,104 --> 00:11:19,184
What I mean by mission, um, you know, the only point why we fly spacecraft to space is to collect some data, right?

82
00:11:19,374 --> 00:11:20,548
Otherwise, there's no point.

83
00:11:21,326 --> 00:11:27,300
Unless we are talking about human exploration because we want to have people out there, because we want to push the limits.

84
00:11:27,504 --> 00:11:28,944
But otherwise, it's the data.

85
00:11:29,424 --> 00:11:32,704
We do some scientific measurements, observations, things like that.

86
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:36,100
We need to collect their data and get it back to Earth.

87
00:11:36,622 --> 00:11:58,704
So when it comes to this, uh again, payload software is special kind of software which is actually doing all these measurements and uh and uh the science operations, and then it's the data collection, data processing, compression, and distribution back to Earth, or maybe storing it on board and then sending it by antennas back to Earth.

88
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:06,788
So overall, um flight software is basically kind of a brain of spacecraft, right?

89
00:12:07,424 --> 00:12:10,148
It coordinates all the subsystems there.

90
00:12:10,606 --> 00:12:17,984
